# Kit Diagram Filter Mechanism

## Core Finding: Filter Logic in visibleGuids (Line 7608+)
The diagram filtering is **NOT** a parameter in `buildKitDiagramData()`. Instead, filtering happens **AFTER** `buildKitDiagramData()` creates all nodes.

## 1. Filter Configuration & Default Values

**Source**: URL search parameters
```typescript
// Line 7619 (Diagram Window)
const selectedKinds = useMemo(() => new Set(searchParams.getAll("kind") as ArtifactKind[]), [searchParams]);

// Line 4321 (Design View)
const selectedKindsFromUrl = useMemo(() => searchParams.getAll("kind") as ArtifactKind[], [searchParams]);
const selectedKinds = useMemo(() => new Set(selectedKindsFromUrl), [selectedKindsFromUrl]);
```

**Default Behavior**: When URL has no `kind` parameters:
- `selectedKinds.size === 0` 
- **Result: ALL node kinds shown** (types, designs, folders, etc.)

## 2. The Actual Filter Logic (Line 7656)

Located inside `visibleGuids` useMemo in the `isRowVisible` function:

```typescript
const isRowVisible = (rowId: string, parentRowId: string | undefined, name: string, kind: ArtifactKind): boolean => {
  if (searchLower && !name.toLowerCase().includes(searchLower)) return false;
  if (selectedKinds.size > 0 && !selectedKinds.has(kind)) return false;  // ← THE FILTER
  return isAncestorChainExpanded(rowId, parentRowId);
};
```

**Logic**: 
- If `selectedKinds.size === 0` → skip kind check, show all
- If `selectedKinds.size > 0` → only include nodes where `selectedKinds.has(kind)`

## 3. How Filtering Applies to Diagram (Line 7736)

```typescript
const filteredNodes = rfNodes.filter((n) => visibleGuids.has(n.data.guid))
```

- `buildKitDiagramData()` creates ALL nodes (types, designs, folders, etc.)
- `visibleGuids` Set only contains guids that pass the `isRowVisible` filter
- Diagram only renders nodes whose guid is in `visibleGuids`

## 4. Toolbar Toggles → Filter State

Line 4356-4364 (Toolbar):
```typescript
<Toggle 
  pressed={selectedKinds.has("designs")} 
  onPressedChange={() => toggleKind("designs")} 
  id="compose.sketchpad.app.kit.toolbar.showDesigns" 
/>
<Toggle 
  pressed={selectedKinds.has("types")} 
  onPressedChange={() => toggleKind("types")} 
  id="compose.sketchpad.app.kit.toolbar.showTypes" 
/>
<Toggle 
  pressed={selectedKinds.has("folders")} 
  onPressedChange={() => toggleKind("folders")} 
  id="compose.sketchpad.app.kit.toolbar.showFolders" 
/>
```

- Toggle `id` matches toolbar.show* constants
- `toggleKind()` modifies URL search params

## 5. toggleKind() Implementation (Line 4324 & 6216)

```typescript
const toggleKind = (kind: ArtifactKind) => {
  const newParams = new URLSearchParams(searchParams);
  const kinds = newParams.getAll("kind") as ArtifactKind[];

  if (kinds.length === 0) {
    newParams.append("kind", kind);  // First click: show ONLY this kind
  } else if (kinds.includes(kind)) {
    const remaining = kinds.filter((k) => k !== kind);
    newParams.delete("kind");
    remaining.forEach((k) => newParams.append("kind", k));  // Remove kind from filter
  } else {
    newParams.append("kind", kind);  // Add kind to filter
  }

  newParams.delete("name");
  newParams.delete("variant");
  newParams.delete("view");
  setSearchParams(newParams);
};
```

**Toggle Behavior**:
1. First click with empty filters: Selects ONLY that kind
2. Click existing kind: Deselects it
3. Click new kind: Adds it to existing selection

## Summary of Why Only Folders Show
When types/designs aren't showing in diagram:
1. Check URL for `kind=` parameters
2. If present (e.g., `kind=folders`), only folders render
3. If absent, all kinds should show, but might be filtered by search term or tree expansion

